    "updated_at": "2022-01-24T21:55:21Z",
    "body": "A `finally()` method guaranteed to be called (like the opposite of `start()`) would be good. I do find it a bit surprising that `abort()` is not called when a `WritableStream` throws from one of its underlying sink methods, or calls `controller.error()`.",
